CREA v3.1  —  n8n Hands Layer
3.1.0 · 2026-09-10

A standalone, self-healing WhatsApp AI booking assistant + shoot-ops automations, run by
the owner on their own Mac and their own accounts.

Install:  INSTALL.md         (one-time setup, ~1 hour — mostly account signups + downloads)
Operate:  OPERATIONS.md      (changes, updates, features, backup, recovery — day two onward)
Booking:  BOOKING.md         (the two decisions: how it prices, what it reads back)
Resilience & security:  COUNTERMEASURES.md
Deploy:   ./go-live.sh       (Docker Compose — n8n + WAHA + vault-api, one command)

What v3.1 adds over v3 (purely additive — every new switch defaults to v3 behaviour)
- Property intake: the assistant asks bedrooms, bathrooms, car spaces, levels, land/floor m²,
  pool (+ size), and free-text features (verandas, backyards, storage, extra kitchens…),
  one question at a time, before it reads the booking back.
- Pricing, 3 modes (CREA_PRICING_MODE): defer (never quotes — default), packages (rough range),
  calculator (a real figure from knowledge/pricing.json).
- Readback + confirm: the assistant summarises the booking and only proceeds on an explicit
  "yes". CREA_CONFIRM_MODE = booking_only (details only) or with_price (includes the estimate).
- Hold → owner confirms → Acuity (CREA_AUTO_BOOK=hold): a confirmed booking is HELD and the
  owner gets a one-tap CONFIRM <ref> / DECLINE <ref>. On CONFIRM, n8n creates the real Acuity
  appointment and tells the customer. CREA_AUTO_BOOK=off keeps the v3 "hand the owner a lead".
- CREA voice ("JARVIS") compatibility: job/lead/client notes are also written in CREA's native
  frontmatter into Jobs/ Clients/ Leads/, so "hey CREA, when's my next booking / confirm
  booking 4A2 / message the Smith client" all work off the same memory.

16 workflows. Verified end to end against a live model on n8n 2.30.7 — see TEST-REPORT.md.
